version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-10"
abstract: >-
  BRAIN is a provider-independent persistent reality, continuity, evidence, authority and
  verification layer for AI and machine systems. It separates four steps that are commonly
  collapsed: intelligence proposes, evidence establishes, authority decides, and reality
  verifies. Records are append-only and superseded rather than edited; belief is resolved on
  read rather than stored; authority is domain-scoped rather than globally ranked; and
  outbound data crosses one enforcement point that decides before any connection opens. This
  public repository is a controlled architecture export at classification
  GENERAL_ARCHITECTURE_CANDIDATE, with an architecture gate of 9 of 9 criteria established. It
  is not the complete development repository, and it is not a claim of production readiness.
